271
00:11:02,667 --> 00:11:04,933
- [Servo] Indiana wants me.

272
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:07,267
- It's Uncle Ben, honey.

273
00:11:07,267 --> 00:11:09,367
Must be an accident
or something.

274
00:11:09,367 --> 00:11:10,767
- [Mike] Yee-haw!

275
00:11:13,233 --> 00:11:15,233
- [Crow] Honey not here.

276
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:20,333
- [Servo] Boy, you
newlyweds are randy.

277
00:11:20,333 --> 00:11:22,433
Now stop it in there!

278
00:11:22,433 --> 00:11:24,467
- There's a plane crash down
the road a couple of miles.

279
00:11:24,467 --> 00:11:26,267
I'm gonna be a little
shorthand 'til help gets here.

280
00:11:26,267 --> 00:11:27,833
Pull around back of me.

281
00:11:30,133 --> 00:11:32,800
- [Mike] Go on about
your marriage, nothin'
happenin' here.

282
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:35,800
(snare drum march)
(Servo imitating music)

283
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:38,367
- [Servo] This is
the army, Mr. Jones.

284
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:41,867
- Come along, both of you.

285
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:48,633
- [Crow] Annette
Funicello wore khakis.

286
00:11:48,633 --> 00:11:49,933
- Get in, honey.

287
00:11:49,933 --> 00:11:51,667
- [Mike] You have the
right to remain mine.

288
00:11:52,867 --> 00:11:55,933
- [Servo] Okay, now get
out, honey. (laughing)

289
00:11:55,933 --> 00:11:57,733
- [Mike] So anyway, we
didn't see much of the Dells.

290
00:11:57,733 --> 00:12:00,233
But we saw the House on
the Rock, which was neat.

291
00:12:02,367 --> 00:12:04,433
(monster screeching)
(Servo imitating monster)

292
00:12:04,433 --> 00:12:07,067
- [Crow] Ha, still goin'.

293
00:12:07,067 --> 00:12:09,000
- [Servo] Well it is creeping,
you've gotta give it that.

294
00:12:11,633 --> 00:12:13,100
- [Mike] Well, it turns
out the creeping terror

295
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:15,367
likes to frolic in
the field. (giggles)

296
00:12:15,367 --> 00:12:16,833
- [Servo] Lollygagging.

297
00:12:16,833 --> 00:12:18,200
- [Crow] I think he's
attracted to that foliage.

298
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:22,033
- [Servo] Power walking
just isn't his thing.

299
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,833
- [Mike] Hey, if it landed
right in Sunset Strip,

300
00:12:26,833 --> 00:12:29,033
he wouldn't be out of
place, am I right here?

301
00:12:29,033 --> 00:12:30,667
(all laughing)

302
00:12:30,667 --> 00:12:33,433
- [Crow] I think he's
self-conscious about
his big ol' butt.

303
00:12:35,233 --> 00:12:36,700
- [Servo] Well anyway,
I like being married,

304
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:41,200
although I do wish he'd go
home at some point. (giggling)

305
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:46,133
- [Crow] Would you
two stop makin' out,

306
00:12:46,133 --> 00:12:47,867
we've got an
investigation to do!

307
00:12:47,867 --> 00:12:49,433
- [Narrator] At the
location of the crash,

308
00:12:49,433 --> 00:12:51,300
they discovered Jeff's truck,

309
00:12:51,300 --> 00:12:53,767
but Jeff himself was not around.

310
00:12:53,767 --> 00:12:56,033
They proceeded with
their investigation.

311
00:12:56,033 --> 00:12:57,367
- [Mike] Oh, I'm the narrator.

312
00:12:57,367 --> 00:13:00,400
I was just on break,
I hope you don't mind.

313
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:02,500
- [Servo] Yep, it's
a truck all right.

314
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,567
It's in park, I'll
put that in my report.

315
00:13:09,667 --> 00:13:10,800
- [Mike] Well, county government

316
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:12,667
was just getting
organized at this point.

317
00:13:14,033 --> 00:13:15,433
- [Crow] Well, I
don't understand it

318
00:13:15,433 --> 00:13:16,933
so let's start shootin'.

319
00:13:16,933 --> 00:13:20,033
- [Narrator] They looked at
the rocket in utter amazement.

320
00:13:20,033 --> 00:13:22,500
- [Servo] It looks like
a Ticonderoga number two.

321
00:13:24,067 --> 00:13:26,167
- [Narrator] A puzzled
Ben finally asked Martin

322
00:13:26,167 --> 00:13:27,667
