323
00:13:27,667 --> 00:13:29,400
- [Mike] Martin
panicked and froze.

324
00:13:30,333 --> 00:13:31,733
- It's no airplane.

325
00:13:31,733 --> 00:13:33,967
- [Crow] Ben never asked
Martin another question.

326
00:13:33,967 --> 00:13:35,667
- Could be one of our missiles.

327
00:13:35,667 --> 00:13:37,700
- [Servo] This county
has missiles, sir?

328
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:39,000
- Or one of theirs.

329
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,200
- [Mike] Shh, honey, no.

330
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:42,600
- You could be right, honey.

331
00:13:43,733 --> 00:13:45,233
I don't think we have
anything this big.

332
00:13:45,233 --> 00:13:46,833
- [Mike] I know that
from our wedding night.

333
00:13:46,833 --> 00:13:49,433
(all laughing)

334
00:13:51,333 --> 00:13:52,867
- [Crow] Well, whatever it is,

335
00:13:52,867 --> 00:13:54,667
it appears to have lowered
their intelligence level!

336
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:57,233
- [Servo] You know, if I
could find a windshield,

337
00:13:57,233 --> 00:13:59,733
I'd give it a ticket. (laughs)

338
00:13:59,733 --> 00:14:00,567
Sheriff.

339
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:05,767
- [Mike] Where's that one guy,

340
00:14:05,767 --> 00:14:06,900
the, whatcha call
it, narrator guy?

341
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:08,733
Hey, buddy!

342
00:14:11,333 --> 00:14:12,733
- [Narrator] Ben
could not understand

343
00:14:12,733 --> 00:14:15,100
