severely damaged.

344
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:16,433
- [Crow] He started crying.

345
00:14:19,733 --> 00:14:21,467
(Servo and Crow gasp)

346
00:14:21,467 --> 00:14:22,800
- [Servo] Wait, I've been here.

347
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:23,667
I'm dead!

348
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:27,667
- [Mike] Apparently Dan
Blocker had been there.

349
00:14:29,700 --> 00:14:32,400
- [Servo] What kind of a
man-beast would wear this?

350
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:33,833
- This hat belongs
to Jeff Peters.

351
00:14:33,833 --> 00:14:35,733
- [Mike] Oh, it's
Jeff Peters' rocket.

352
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,633
- Jeff!

353
00:14:38,633 --> 00:14:41,100
Jeff, Jeff are ya in there?

354
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:42,600
- [Crow] Uh, yeah,
uh, can it wait?

355
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:45,467
- Martin, go back to my
car and get my flashlight.

356
00:14:46,633 --> 00:14:49,600
- [Servo] I'll just
pout. (whimpering)

357
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:52,367
(new wave music)

358
00:14:55,633 --> 00:14:58,300
(Servo panting)

359
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:02,600
- [Mike] So you pretty
serious about your husband?

360
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:03,933
Uh, no, you're--

361
00:15:03,933 --> 00:15:06,900
- [Servo] Guh, what's
my time? (panting)

362
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:14,433
- Ben, don't go in there.

363
00:15:14,433 --> 00:15:16,333
You don't know what's in there.

364
00:15:16,333 --> 00:15:17,900
- [Mike] Go, go, go, go, go.

365
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:19,133
- [Crow] Go.

366
00:15:19,133 --> 00:15:20,833
- I think I hear
it moving inside.

367
00:15:20,833 --> 00:15:21,700
Maybe he's hurt.

368
00:15:23,633 --> 00:15:25,500
- [Servo] I gotta
check under the movie.

369
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:28,100
Oh yeah, this is a big
mess under here, jeez.

370
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,633
- Ben, please don't.

371
00:15:31,633 --> 00:15:32,467
- [Crow] Go.

372
00:15:32,467 --> 00:15:33,333
(monster screeching)

373
00:15:33,333 --> 00:15:34,200
- [Servo] Oo.

374
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,833
(explosion)

375
00:15:35,833 --> 00:15:38,133
- [Crow] (laughs) That old
gag, exploding flashlight!

376
00:15:38,133 --> 00:15:39,067
- Ben.

377
00:15:39,067 --> 00:15:40,233
(monster screeching)

378
00:15:40,233 --> 00:15:41,433
- [Mike] He almost
showed an emotion there.

379
00:15:42,933 --> 00:15:45,267
- [Servo] Honey, we gotta go
open the gifts at mom's house.

380
00:15:45,267 --> 00:15:46,533
(Brett screaming)

381
00:15:46,533 --> 00:15:49,233
(monster screeching)
(Ben screaming)

382
00:15:49,233 --> 00:15:51,133
- [Servo] Doesn't sound good.

383
00:15:51,133 --> 00:15:52,567
(monster screeching)
(Ben screaming)

384
00:15:52,567 --> 00:15:56,367
- [Mike] Well, he probably
knows what he's doing. (laughs)

385
00:15:56,367 --> 00:15:57,633
- [Servo] This is the
worst honeymoon I've ever,

386
00:15:57,633 --> 00:16:01,800
oh, it's my first
honeymoon! (laughs)

387
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:04,900
- [Crow] I know he'd want us
to take the sheriff's car.

388
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:06,433
- Car one, calling in.

389
00:16:06,433 --> 00:16:07,867
- [Mike] Reporting
large steering wheel.

390
00:16:07,867 --> 00:16:09,367
- Car one, calling in.

391
00:16:09,367 --> 00:16:11,567
- [Servo] I have some bad
news and some bad news.

392
00:16:13,067 --> 00:16:14,600
(snare drum)

393
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:17,533
- [Crow] Here comes the Rocori
Sauk Rapids High School Band!

394
00:16:17,533 --> 00:16:18,733
- [Narrator] Within the hour,

395
00:16:18,733 --> 00:16:20,067
Martin's unusual
call for assistance

396
00:16:20,067 --> 00:16:22,400
was answered by a special unit

397
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:24,800
led by a Colonel James Caldwell.

398
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:27,167
- [Servo] We're the
special unit, hello!

399
00:16:27,167 --> 00:16:29,000
(Crow laughing)

400
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,200
- [Mike] It took about an hour.

401
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,833
They stopped at
Hardee's on the way.

402
00:16:31,833 --> 00:16:34,167
(snare drum)
(Servo imitating trumpet)

403
00:16:34,167 --> 00:16:35,300
- [Colonel] Let's get going.

404
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:36,467
- [Crow] There is a branch.

405
00:16:36,467 --> 00:16:38,467
This is not a drill.

406
00:16:38,467 --> 00:16:40,533
- [Colonel] Let's go,
let's go, move it over.

407
00:16:40,533 --> 00:16:41,767
Let's get going.

408
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:46,833
- [Servo] Ah, yes, the days
of rampant military spending.

409
00:16:46,833 --> 00:16:48,233
- [Colonel] All right, back
on the truck, let's go.

410
00:16:49,433 --> 00:16:51,333
- [Mike] We push more
logs before 9:00 a.m.

411
00:16:51,333 --> 00:16:53,067
than most people do all day!

412
00:16:53,067 --> 00:16:55,833
(snare drum and piano)

413
00:16:55,833 --> 00:16:57,233
- [Crow] They popped
a little Dave Brubeck

414
00:16:57,233 --> 00:16:58,867
into the tape deck.

415
00:16:58,867 --> 00:17:00,067
- [Servo] Just by
moving that tree,

416
00:17:00,067 --> 00:17:01,900
an owl has lost its habitat.

417
00:17:01,900 --> 00:17:05,167
(snare drum and piano)

418
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:10,000
- [Mike] Rose said
Sharon's havin' a baby!

419
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,933
(trumpet fanfare)
(Servo imitating trumpet)

420
00:17:12,933 --> 00:17:14,967
- [Crow] Aw, somebody
took our campsite.

421
00:17:17,933 --> 00:17:20,833
- [Servo] Okay, guys,
don't frag me again.

422
00:17:20,833 --> 00:17:22,667
- [Colonel] Sergeant, take
one man and check it out.

423
00:17:22,667 --> 00:17:23,600
- Yes, sir.

424
00:17:23,600 --> 00:17:24,533
- [Crow] 'Cause we're special!

425
00:17:24,533 --> 00:17:25,367
- Okay.

426
00:17:26,567 --> 00:17:27,600
- [Mike] Uh, should we go?

427
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:28,933
I think he wants us to go.

428
00:17:30,033 --> 00:17:34,467
- [Servo] (whimpering)
I'm a-scared.

429
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:37,333
- [Crow] I'll go first.

430
00:17:37,333 --> 00:17:39,433
After he's done eating
me, Joe, you go in.

431
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:41,500
Sooner or later,
indigestion will set in.

432
00:17:45,067 --> 00:17:47,700
- [Mike] More troops are
sent in to fix the manifold.

433
00:17:52,333 --> 00:17:55,133
(Crow chewing and slurping)

434
00:17:55,133 --> 00:17:56,067
- [Servo] Ah, the
original concept

435
00:17:56,067 --> 00:17:58,100
for the Iwo Jima sculpture.

436
00:17:58,100 --> 00:18:01,000
(electronic frequency
and beeping)

437
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,033
- [Mike] They're
gonna force earthlings

438
00:18:02,033 --> 00:18:03,400
to read their gas meters!

439
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,700
(Crow gasps)

440
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:09,300
(machinery beeping)
(Servo beeping)

441
00:18:09,300 --> 00:18:11,767
- [Crow] Aw great, a race
of ham radio operators.

442
00:18:13,167 --> 00:18:15,367
- [Servo] Yes, this
can all be yours!

443
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:19,467
(machinery beeping)
(Servo beeping)

444
00:18:19,467 --> 00:18:21,567
- [Mike] Well, they've
perfected the dial.

445
00:18:24,433 --> 00:18:26,700
- [Crow] Are we inside
Television City?

446
00:18:29,433 --> 00:18:32,200
- [Servo] And back again
in case we missed anything.

447
00:18:33,367 --> 00:18:34,800
- [Mike] The prices
on these Kenwoods!

448
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:36,800
The aliens must be insane!

449
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:38,000
(monster roaring)

450
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:39,833
- [Servo] (gasps) It's
conglomerate rock!

451
00:18:41,933 --> 00:18:44,600
- [Mike] Oh please, just
five more minutes, Mom.

452
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:47,133
(purposeful music)

453
00:18:47,133 --> 00:18:48,467
- [Crow] If there's a whole
bunch of dials in there,

454
00:18:48,467 --> 00:18:49,533
I'll be so jealous.

455
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:54,200
- [Servo] There's the aliens,
shoot 'em! (imitating gunfire)

456
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:55,333
- [Narrator] The
sergeant reported seeing

457
00:18:55,333 --> 00:18:57,200
an amazingly large creature

458
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:59,233
in the aft section
of the strange craft.

459
00:18:59,233 --> 00:19:00,700
- [Mike] He thought
it was Boog Powell.

460
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,333
- [Narrator] Further
reported that it was secured

461
00:19:02,333 --> 00:19:04,633
by a kind of metal harness,

462
00:19:04,633 --> 00:19:07,467
but that the creature could
still move around somewhat,

463
00:19:07,467 --> 00:19:10,433
and for that reason, they had
not gotten too close to it.

464
00:19:10,433 --> 00:19:11,700
- [Crow] Plus, they're yeller.

465
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:13,333
- [Narrator] No trace
of either Ben or Jeff

466
00:19:13,333 --> 00:19:14,767
- [Servo] Or Akbar.

467
00:19:14,767 --> 00:19:16,067
- [Narrator] The colonel
ordered continuous guard duty

468
00:19:16,067 --> 00:19:17,467
around the spaceship

469
00:19:17,467 --> 00:19:20,267
and decided to set up a
temporary military headquarters

470
00:19:20,267 --> 00:19:21,767
at the sheriff's office in town.

471
00:19:21,767 --> 00:19:24,900
- [Mike] It was a brilliant
strategic maneuver.

472
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:26,200
- [Crow] Yes, sir.

473
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:27,033
Jagoff.

474
00:19:28,633 --> 00:19:30,867
- [Servo] Back at the high
school, shop class was canceled.

475
00:19:30,867 --> 00:19:32,133
- [Narrator] By the next day,

476
00:19:32,133 --> 00:19:34,400
Colonel Caldwell had the
situation well in hand.

477
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:35,633
- [Mike] K.D. Lang!

478
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:37,100
- [Narrator] He had
called Washington

479
00:19:37,100 --> 00:19:39,867
and received his orders from
the highest possible authority.

480
00:19:39,867 --> 00:19:41,100
- [Servo] God.

481
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:42,800
- [Narrator] He was to
maintain tight security

482
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:45,267
and to await the arrival
of a Dr. Bradford,

483
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:46,767
who had been on assignment

484
00:19:46,767 --> 00:19:50,033
at the Jodrell Bank Radio
Observatory in England.

485
00:19:50,033 --> 00:19:53,100
Upon arrival, Bradford was
to take complete charge

486
00:19:53,100 --> 00:19:54,167
of the operation.

487
00:19:54,167 --> 00:19:55,667
- [Crow] Constant craving.

488
00:19:55,667 --> 00:19:56,467
- [Narrator] He was the
world's leading authority

489
00:19:56,467 --> 00:19:57,467
on space emissions.

490
00:19:57,467 --> 00:19:58,700
- Yuck.
- Eeugh.

491
00:19:58,700 --> 00:19:59,633
He had worked out
a series of systems

492
00:19:59,633 --> 00:20:01,200
that might lead to communication

493
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:03,100
with other forms of life.

494
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:05,800
When, as, and if
they were contacted.

495
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:06,733
- [Mike] Preposition city!

496
00:20:06,733 --> 00:20:07,967
- [Narrator] Martin was outraged

497
00:20:07,967 --> 00:20:09,900
by the government's
intellectual approach

498
00:20:09,900 --> 00:20:11,800
to a monster that
had already killed

499
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:14,433
and caused the disappearance
of his two close friends.

500
00:20:14,433 --> 00:20:16,000
- [Servo] Not since the
Lincoln-Douglas debate.

501
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,900
- [Narrator] Caldwell
tended to agree with him,

502
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:19,800
but stated he had to
follow his orders.

503
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:21,200
- [Crow] It was a real
interesting conversation.

504
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:22,700
- [Narrator] One of those orders

505
00:20:22,700 --> 00:20:25,867
was to suppress the news of
the death of Ben and Jeff.

506
00:20:25,867 --> 00:20:28,300
Martin was appointed
temporary sheriff

507
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:30,700
and all news intended
for public consumption

508
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,533
was to emanate from his office.

509
00:20:32,533 --> 00:20:33,933
- [Servo] What's
emanate mean, sir?

510
00:20:33,933 --> 00:20:35,467
- [Narrator] The Air Authority
issued a coverup story

511
00:20:35,467 --> 00:20:37,567
that a plane had
crashed and burned,

512
00:20:37,567 --> 00:20:39,233
and this was to suffice

513
00:20:39,233 --> 00:20:41,200
until the experts
cleared up the mystery

514
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:43,233
of the visitor from outer space.

515
00:20:43,233 --> 00:20:46,200
- [Mike] Then they went on to
plot the Bay of Pigs Invasion.

516
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:49,067
- [Crow] Hey,
welcome to the show.

517
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:52,267
- [Narrator] In a remote
section of the county,

518
00:20:52,267 --> 00:20:54,733
the first of a series
of tragedies took place.

519
00:20:54,733 --> 00:20:56,233
- [Servo] Two ladies!

520
00:20:56,233 --> 00:20:57,200
- [Narrator] Tragedies that
would have been avoided

521
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:58,367
had the public been warned.

522
00:20:58,367 --> 00:21:00,800
(monster roaring)

523
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:03,533
- [Mike] Is she really
going out with him?

524
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,200
- [Crow] Oh great, the
monster's a voyeur.

525
00:21:09,867 --> 00:21:11,233
- [Servo] You know,

526
00:21:11,233 --> 00:21:12,300
this is how all
teenagers see themselves.

527
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:13,400
Poor kids.

528
00:21:14,533 --> 00:21:15,800
- [Mike] The unbearable
whiteness of being.

529
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:17,100
(Servo laughing)

530
00:21:17,100 --> 00:21:18,800
- [Crow] I'll be
there in about an hour

531
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:20,233
if you can just bear with me.

532
00:21:21,733 --> 00:21:24,000
- [Servo] (moaning)

533
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,733
Oh, Jerry, you wild animal!
(monster roaring)

534
00:21:26,733 --> 00:21:28,567
Eh, eh, huh?

535
00:21:28,567 --> 00:21:30,600
- [Mike] Oh my God, it's my dad!

536
00:21:33,567 --> 00:21:35,067
- [Crow] We have to
get out of here, honey.

537
00:21:35,067 --> 00:21:37,733
We only have an hour to eat,
have sex, and then leave.

538
00:21:37,733 --> 00:21:40,567
(monster roaring)

539
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:43,467
- [Mike] Uh, come on, honey.

540
00:21:43,467 --> 00:21:44,767
Let's crab walk outta here.

541
00:21:46,133 --> 00:21:47,700
(woman screaming)
(monster roaring)

542
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:49,467
- [Servo] Could you at least
not eat my bathing suit,

543
00:21:49,467 --> 00:21:50,767
it's brand new.

544
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:53,900
(woman screaming)
(monster roaring)

545
00:21:53,900 --> 00:21:55,733
- [Mike] You have a kind face.

546
00:21:56,933 --> 00:21:58,700
- [Crow] You're lucky
you have thick hair!

547
00:21:58,700 --> 00:22:03,667
(woman screaming)
(monster roaring)

548
00:22:04,533 --> 00:22:05,500
- [Servo] Well, he's not shy,

549
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:06,967
you can say that much about him.

550
00:22:06,967 --> 00:22:08,700
(Crow and Mike laughing)

551
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:10,800
- [Mike] Hey, if you could
help me out by climbin' in...

552
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:13,733
(Crow and Servo laughing)

553
00:22:13,733 --> 00:22:15,733
- [Crow] 'Twas
beauty fed the beast.

554
00:22:15,733 --> 00:22:18,467
- [Servo] Wow!
(monster screaming)

555
00:22:18,467 --> 00:22:21,500
Always fun to cook for,
'cause he enjoys eating!

556
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:23,900
(monster screaming)

557
00:22:23,900 --> 00:22:25,767
- [Mike] Oh, the legs are
always the last to go.

558
00:22:25,767 --> 00:22:27,100
- [Servo] Mm hm.

559
00:22:28,467 --> 00:22:30,367
- [Crow] Would you eat
like a human being, please?

560
00:22:30,367 --> 00:22:31,700
This is so rude!

561
00:22:32,833 --> 00:22:34,467
- [Servo] Ah, needs
some seasoning!

562
00:22:34,467 --> 00:22:36,333
- [Mike] Last time
I eat Norwegian.

563
00:22:36,333 --> 00:22:39,733
(woman screaming)
(dramatic music)

564
00:22:39,733 --> 00:22:42,800
- [Servo] Earth girls
are greazy. (laughs)

565
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:47,900
- [Mike] Oh wait, it's
Lent, I swore off girls!

566
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:48,700
Oh well.

567
00:22:50,100 --> 00:22:52,667
- [Crow] I can't believe
I ate the whole thing.

568
00:22:52,667 --> 00:22:54,700
- [Servo] You ate it, Ralph.

569
00:22:54,700 --> 00:22:57,300
Good goin' down but, oh,
then they just sit there.

570
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:59,833
(spaceship beeping)

571
00:22:59,833 --> 00:23:02,000
- [Mike] I love you, spaceship.

572
00:23:04,167 --> 00:23:05,433
(all yell in surprise)

573
00:23:05,433 --> 00:23:06,700
- [Servo] Wow.

574
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:07,533
- [Mike] It's the
creeping newlywed.

575
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:13,533
- [Crow] I have no
idea what I'm doing.

576
00:23:13,533 --> 00:23:16,033
- [Servo] All you dials
and gauges, I'm in charge.

577
00:23:17,167 --> 00:23:18,433
- [Mike] At this point,

578
00:23:18,433 --> 00:23:20,567
the director attempted
an arty sort of shot.

579
00:23:21,833 --> 00:23:23,733
(Servo laughing)

580
00:23:23,733 --> 00:23:26,233
- [Crow] That other monster
must be the opener for this one.

581
00:23:26,233 --> 00:23:27,467
- [Mike] Oh yeah.

582
00:23:27,467 --> 00:23:29,367
- [Servo] Danger,
danger, Will Robinson!

583
00:23:29,367 --> 00:23:32,200
(monster roaring)

584
00:23:34,633 --> 00:23:39,633
(spaceship ambience)
(doors closing)

585
00:23:48,600 --> 00:23:51,033
- Oh Mike, you know
that California flag?

586
00:23:51,033 --> 00:23:53,300
The one with the
goofy looking' bear?

587
00:23:53,300 --> 00:23:54,600
- California grizzly bear.

588
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:55,433
They're extinct, you know.

589
00:23:55,433 --> 00:23:56,933
- Oh, too bad.

590
00:23:56,933 --> 00:23:58,333
Anyway, I was thinkin',

591
00:23:58,333 --> 00:24:01,267
we are many and yet we are one

592
00:24:01,267 --> 00:24:04,367
here on the Satellite of
Love, just like California.

593
00:24:04,367 --> 00:24:06,800
And so I made us a flag!

594
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:07,633
And Mike?

595
00:24:07,633 --> 00:24:08,467
- Yes?

596
00:24:08,467 --> 00:24:09,733
- Hut ti tup!

597
00:24:09,733 --> 00:24:12,067
- Mike, would you
help us raise it?

598
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:13,867
- Yes.

599
00:24:13,867 --> 00:24:14,833
(laughing)

600
00:24:14,833 --> 00:24:15,767
Okay.

601
00:24:15,767 --> 00:24:17,000
(Servo imitating snare drum)

602
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:20,067
- I pledge allegiance
to the flag

603
00:24:20,067 --> 00:24:22,200
of the Satellite of Love,

604
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:25,600
free, united, glorious, fruited,

605
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:27,233
that grand bi-lobed orb,

606
00:24:27,233 --> 00:24:29,533
born of the loins
of our founder,

607
00:24:29,533 --> 00:24:31,933
Jacques du Bourgoin
One Eye Canapadidiwa,

608
00:24:31,933 --> 00:24:34,833
farmer, claims adjuster, rebel

609
00:24:34,833 --> 00:24:38,400
with alabaster symmetry and
golden grains of Xanadu!

610
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:41,633
One satellite under God, or not,

611
00:24:41,633 --> 00:24:46,500
indirigible, with liberty
and justice for all.

612
00:24:46,500 --> 00:24:47,433
Thank you.

613
00:24:47,433 --> 00:24:48,567
(pop gun pops)

614
00:24:48,567 --> 00:24:50,200
Oh, one last thing, Michael.

615
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:51,667
Check your nightstand.

616
00:24:51,667 --> 00:24:54,367
You'll find a cyanide capsule
in case we're ever taken.

617
00:24:54,367 --> 00:24:55,867
- I'm not taking cyanide.

618
00:24:55,867 --> 00:24:57,533
- Aren't you one of us, Mike?

619
00:24:57,533 --> 00:24:58,967
- Well, cyanide goes
to my hips. (laughs)

620
00:24:58,967 --> 00:25:00,533
- A Tory, eh!

621
00:25:00,533 --> 00:25:01,667
Outsider!

622
00:25:01,667 --> 00:25:02,767
Revenges!

623
00:25:02,767 --> 00:25:04,133
Provocateur!
- We'll be right back.

624
00:25:04,133 --> 00:25:05,700
- Do you not know

625
00:25:05,700 --> 00:25:07,567
that you have only one
live to live as a plant?

626
00:25:07,567 --> 00:25:09,500
Give me liberty or kill me!

627
00:25:09,500 --> 00:25:10,300
- [Crow] Hm?

628
00:25:10,300 --> 00:25:11,400
- [Servo] Hey, my hat.

629
00:25:12,867 --> 00:25:15,433
- [Mike] I'm not, no,
no, I'm not going.

630
00:25:15,433 --> 00:25:16,933
- [Crow] Red, commie.

631
00:25:16,933 --> 00:25:18,400
- [Narrator] While they
were awaiting the arrival

632
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:20,100
of Dr. Bradford, Martin
instructed Barney,

633
00:25:20,100 --> 00:25:21,900
on advice from Colonel Caldwell

634
00:25:21,900 --> 00:25:24,033
to plant in the
local papers the news

635
00:25:24,033 --> 00:25:27,400
that Ben and Jeff had
taken off on a fishing trip

636
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:28,967
to British Columbia.

637
00:25:28,967 --> 00:25:31,067
The Colonel had impressed
the bereaved families

638
00:25:31,067 --> 00:25:33,467
with the necessity of
maintaining secrecy,

639
00:25:33,467 --> 00:25:36,033
and these brave
relatives had agreed.

640
00:25:36,033 --> 00:25:37,267
- [Mike] After being beaten.

641
00:25:37,267 --> 00:25:38,100
- [Servo] Oo.

642
00:25:40,400 --> 00:25:43,367
So, should we have at it
again, honey? (laughs)

643
00:25:43,367 --> 00:25:46,300
- [Crow] Well, I think you're
a wonderful acting sheriff.

644
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:48,767
- [Narrator] Despite
Brett's inquiries

645
00:25:48,767 --> 00:25:51,667
about what Martin had
seen in the spacecraft,

646
00:25:51,667 --> 00:25:53,533
he avoided specific details

647
00:25:53,533 --> 00:25:55,533
for fear of disturbing
her more than she was.

648
00:25:55,533 --> 00:25:56,767
- [Servo] What's she doing?

649
00:25:56,767 --> 00:25:58,233
- [Narrator] If the
truth were known,

650
00:25:58,233 --> 00:26:00,700
Martin was more than a
little disturbed himself.

651
00:26:00,700 --> 00:26:02,067
- [Mike] Now cough, honey.

652
00:26:02,067 --> 00:26:04,300
- [Narrator] Shortly thereafter,
Dr. Bradford arrived.

653
00:26:05,467 --> 00:26:07,467
- [Crow] I said Dr.
Bradford arrived.

654
00:26:08,633 --> 00:26:09,667
- [Narrator] He was
a much younger man

655
00:26:09,667 --> 00:26:10,900
than one would imagine.

656
00:26:10,900 --> 00:26:12,367
- [Servo] I have
no preconceptions.

657
00:26:12,367 --> 00:26:15,267
- Martin, I'd like for
you to meet Dr. Bradford.

658
00:26:15,267 --> 00:26:16,900
- I've heard a lot about
you from the Colonel.

659
00:26:16,900 --> 00:26:18,500
- Well, nothing bad, I trust.

660
00:26:18,500 --> 00:26:19,967
- [Mike] Handsome, aren't I?

661
00:26:19,967 --> 00:26:21,933
- Martin and his wife
were in the original party

662
00:26:21,933 --> 00:26:23,333
that found the fallen craft.

663
00:26:23,333 --> 00:26:24,533
(Crow laughing)

664
00:26:24,533 --> 00:26:26,033
- I was sorry to hear
about your uncle.

665
00:26:26,033 --> 00:26:27,533
Tough break.

666
00:26:27,533 --> 00:26:28,833
- [Servo] Which one
of us is talking?

667
00:26:28,833 --> 00:26:29,667
- I hope you're feeling better.

668
00:26:29,667 --> 00:26:30,867
- Yes, thank you.

669
00:26:30,867 --> 00:26:32,300
A couple hours of sleep
did a world of good.

670
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:35,167
- Bradford thanks the
colonel for his assistance,

671
00:26:35,167 --> 00:26:37,233
and then asks to
speak to Martin.

672
00:26:37,233 --> 00:26:38,733
- [Servo] Martin, have you
noticed how young I look?

673
00:26:38,733 --> 00:26:40,167
- [Narrator] Bradford
questioned Martin

674
00:26:40,167 --> 00:26:42,267
about everything
that had transpired.

675
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:43,667
- [Mike] Well, we
met and got married.

676
00:26:43,667 --> 00:26:46,200
- [Narrator] To recall
everything in precise detail.

677
00:26:46,200 --> 00:26:47,633
(Servo imitating slap bass)

678
00:26:47,633 --> 00:26:49,600
- [Narrator] Really
didn't have much for him.

679
00:26:49,600 --> 00:26:51,933
The two soldiers that
entered the rocket earlier

680
00:26:51,933 --> 00:26:53,200
had been summoned

681
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:55,600
and Bradford hoped to
learn more from them.

682
00:26:55,600 --> 00:26:57,100
- [Crow] You know, I'm
only 35. (chuckles)

683
00:26:57,100 --> 00:26:58,500
- [Narrator] Would
not enter the rocket

684
00:26:58,500 --> 00:27:00,633
until the arrival of
certain equipment.

685
00:27:00,633 --> 00:27:02,067
- [Servo] And
fresh under things.

686
00:27:02,067 --> 00:27:03,433
- [Narrator] From his
discussion, it was apparent

687
00:27:03,433 --> 00:27:05,700
that the doctor
considered this situation

688
00:27:05,700 --> 00:27:08,167
a magnificent
opportunity for mankind.

689
00:27:08,167 --> 00:27:09,933
- [Mike] He celebrated
with a Chesterfield.

690
00:27:09,933 --> 00:27:10,833
- [Narrator] He felt that
if he could communicate

691
00:27:10,833 --> 00:27:12,233
with the creature,

692
00:27:12,233 --> 00:27:14,967
it might be possible to advance
human knowledge by years

693
00:27:14,967 --> 00:27:16,200
or even centuries.

694
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:17,833
- [Crow] Or maybe
just a few days.

695
00:27:17,833 --> 00:27:18,900
- [Narrator] The spaceship alone

696
00:27:18,900 --> 00:27:20,733
signified an
intellectual development

697
00:27:20,733 --> 00:27:23,000
far in advance of
anything on earth.

698
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:24,233
- [Servo] Especially these two.

699
00:27:24,233 --> 00:27:25,767
- [Narrator] When
Martin asked him

700
00:27:25,767 --> 00:27:28,267
how he intended to protect
himself from the creature,

701
00:27:28,267 --> 00:27:30,200
Bradford said not to worry.

702
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:31,667
- [Crow] Then he slapped him.

703
00:27:31,667 --> 00:27:32,900
- [Narrator] He hadn't
come here to be victimized

704
00:27:32,900 --> 00:27:34,967
either by his own or
the creatures feared.

705
00:27:34,967 --> 00:27:37,233
- [Mike] Go ahead, punch
me in the stomach, come on!

706
00:27:38,733 --> 00:27:41,433
- [Servo] Oh, it's so
fulfilling being married.

707
00:27:43,167 --> 00:27:44,867
- [Mike] There, our one plate.

708
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:48,767
- [Crow] Oh, Martin invited
the alien home for supper

709
00:27:48,767 --> 00:27:50,000
without telling his wife!

710
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:51,400
- [Servo] D'oh!

711
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:54,433
- [Mike] Martin keeps a
softball glove above the stove.

712
00:27:54,433 --> 00:27:56,433
- [Servo] Okay, now it's not
gonna look like meatloaf,

713
00:27:56,433 --> 00:27:57,367
but it is.

714
00:27:57,367 --> 00:27:58,900
She boils it, I don't know why.

715
00:27:58,900 --> 00:28:00,533
Ew.

716
00:28:00,533 --> 00:28:01,500
Eh, just eat.

717
00:28:03,700 --> 00:28:05,367
- [Crow] Oh, she's getting
the breakfast dishes done

718
00:28:05,367 --> 00:28:06,533
just in time.

719
00:28:07,667 --> 00:28:08,500
- [Mike] Hi, honey.

720
00:28:08,500 --> 00:28:09,367
Pregnant yet?

721
00:28:10,600 --> 00:28:12,300
- [Servo] I'm pretty
sure this is my house.

722
00:28:12,300 --> 00:28:13,600
I haven't lived here that long.

723
00:28:13,600 --> 00:28:15,433
Why don't you go in
and check it out?

724
00:28:17,533 --> 00:28:20,333
- [Crow] You grab the stereo,
I'll get the silverware.

725
00:28:20,333 --> 00:28:22,667
- [Mike] Shh, give
me the chloroform.

726
00:28:22,667 --> 00:28:26,233
- [Servo] Ah, the Menendez
brothers come home. (laughs)

727
00:28:27,367 --> 00:28:28,600
- [Crow] It's nice
how they're so playful

728
00:28:28,600 --> 00:28:30,667
after the day's
murder and mayhem.

729
00:28:32,400 --> 00:28:34,067
- [Servo] I hope she comes
out and blows 'em away.

730
00:28:34,067 --> 00:28:36,433
(chuckles)

731
00:28:36,433 --> 00:28:38,200
- [Mike] Love how you
put the medicine cabinet

732
00:28:38,200 --> 00:28:39,633
in the living room.

733
00:28:39,633 --> 00:28:41,800
(easy listening music)

734
